  "A": "issue handshake: go + NEXT fields down, ready back (base issues the cycle ready is seen) -> ot_qfd_issue_shell: RT-edge not-ready window after a go, ready rebuilt from monotone unit state",
  "B": "status / chaining: idle, progress, progress_rows (registered, cleared on the accepting edge) -> masked for the RT window, then post-accept and monotone (stale = conservative)",
  "C": "sampled result: am_idx / am_val / am_any read by the argmax fold on the next AMAX go -> with stations an AMAX op also waits for the engine idle, so am_* are frozen sample-to-accept",
  "D": "memory read loop through the controller (stream unit va read, INT8 embedding decode): fixed 1-edge latency -> decode moved to the stream-unit side (ot_qfd_su_embed); selector a_src travels with the go; token / scale are per-token constants, stationed",
  "E": "clock-enable path: engine ICG (po_me_clk) and its enable me_en / me_clk_en (gates the engine VM write enables and the die scale banks in the same cycle; me_mem_ok feeds it) -> not stationed (clock-gating check); engine-side stations on the gated clock, shell counts engine edges",
  "F": "posted / sticky / observation: fault (sticky), kv_we -> kv_write_flush (idle-qualified with the masked idle), wrom_re/addr (INT8 weights and INT8 embedding: unused, observation) -> delayed is safe",
  "local": "not a controller crossing: the unit's own memory / tree / KV ports (direct, as in the base)"
 },
